  "mn143:3.1": "",
  "mn143:3.2": "The sick Anāthapiṇḍika was consoled by Ānanda at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn55.27/en/sujato#3.2'>SN 55.27:3.2</a> and by Sāriputta at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn55.26/en/sujato#4.2'>SN 55.26:4.2</a>. In other cases, we find the Buddha making such visits to sick monks (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn22.87/en/sujato#2.7'>SN 22.87:2.7</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn22.88/en/sujato#2.8'>SN 22.88:2.8</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn46.14/en/sujato#2.1'>SN 46.14:2.1</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn46.15/en/sujato#2.1'>SN 46.15:2.1</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an6.56/en/sujato#2.1'>AN 6.56:2.1</a>), but for some reason visits to householders are only attested for Sāriputta (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn97/en/sujato#28.2'>MN 97:28.2</a>) or Ānanda (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn47.29/en/sujato#2.2'>SN 47.29:2.2</a>). ",
