  "mn143:5.1": "",
  "mn143:5.2": "The teaching on the six senses typically begins by establishing awareness on the reality of the eye (etc.) as something that is grasped at (eg. <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn145/en/sujato#3.1'>MN 145:3.1</a>). Here Sāriputta skips over this straight to letting go, signifying that his teaching starts with an advanced level of insight. ",
